<article class="env-example" id="0BN8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BN8">Example <span data-tag="0BN8">58.5.1</span>.</a> Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field and $X = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)$. In this case $\textit{FÉt}_ X$ is equivalent to the category of finite sets. This works more generally when $k$ is separably algebraically closed. The reason is that a scheme étale over $k$ is the disjoint union of spectra of fields finite separable over $k$, see Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02GL" data-tag="02GL">29.37.7</a>. </p>
</article>